date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/luisrosa/Mechanistic-Localization-Is-Distribution-Relative"
abstract: >-
  Source, validation code, and submission artifacts for a theory of mechanistic
  localization in which the realized probability state is an explicit argument
  of the localization claim. The paper separates receiver sufficiency from
  context invariance and identifies exact support localization as a zero-loss
  shadow of the distribution-relative problem.
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - neural networks
  - localization
  - circuits
  - distribution shift
  - representation
